A||||8||Carrolles||Finally tried my G-Tech||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||03-29-2001||04:07 PM||||I've been carrying my G-Tech around in my car for three months and the curiosity got to me last night on the way home from AuotZone.<P>I stopped on the side of the road on a two lane county road and waited for traffic to clear.  Was a bit challenging trying to remember how to program the thing while watching for a break in traffic so I could make a run.<P>85SE v-6 4 spd.<BR>Grooms 2.8L stock long block I got from Ed Parks last year.  Now have about 5000 miles on it.<BR>ported intake and exhaust manifolds.<BR>no other mods<P>0 to 60 mph  7.72 seconds<BR>quarter mile 15.98 seconds  85.8 mph<P>By no means a rocket but I'm sure I can do better with practice.  I was breaking loose quite a bit on launch and not pushing the shifting due to shift cables out of adjustment.<P>Sure was fun though.<P>Later,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||03-29-2001||06:23 PM||||bot||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||03-29-2001||07:24 PM||||You convinced me. I gotta have one of those. They charge me here $100 for a dyno run. For $40 more I got my own dyno.<BR>Anyone knows where to get the best deal? Any cupon for the web autoparts?||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||03-29-2001||09:18 PM||||I've been wanting one of those for a while now!  I think once I get my resto done and before I do all my engine mods, I'm going to get one.<P>Ive seen many places $139.95  Even straight from Tesla Electronics.  Still, its cheaper than 2 dyno runs and 1/4 mile runs.  Just plain neat too!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||03-30-2001||09:05 AM||||Check E-bay<P>I got mine from a guy in a Miata club.  My neighbor knew him and that he had one for sale.  I paid $75.00 US.||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||03-30-2001||03:11 PM||||JC whitney was pretty cheap with it... i still dont think it can possibly be accurate, i would have to see one,      what does it say for how much HP you have?<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||04-02-2001||09:05 AM||||The literature lists the following for accuracy:<P>0-60 mph    +/- 1/10 sec<BR>60-0 braking   +/- 2 feet<BR>1/4 mile E.T   +/- 1/10 sec<BR>1/4 mile speed  +/- 1mph<BR>horsepower  +/- 3 HP<BR>Inst. G's   +/- 2/100 G<BR>Cont. G's   +/- 2/100 G<P>I've heard some guys run these at the track and get close to trap results.<P>You need to know vehicle weight to get wheel horsepower.<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||04-02-2001||11:50 AM||||That thing is as accurate as it says. Many (&gt;20) people have compared results with the track times in the Vette forum and it is about 1/10th off all the time. You can't get better than that.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||04-02-2001||04:14 PM||||Granted, a 10th on the quarter mile is a huge difference.  Just look at the distance between two race cars running a 10th apart.  But still, for the money, you can't beat it.  And it gives you a constant to measure changes with.  Can't even to that at the track with weather, different tracks, etc.<BR>I plan on getting one this Spring/Summer.||||reg||1
